# Presentation shell (UITK bus)

Swap or host **display chrome** via `UiPresentationBridge` → projector DTO → `I*Shell.Apply` — without forking gameplay rules or phase HUD orchestration.

**Authority:** [presentation shell implementation](../docs/04-dev/presentation-shell-implementation.md) · [ADR 042](../decisions/042-presentation-bus.md)

**Gotchas (read before implement/review):** [presentation-shell-gotchas.md](../docs/04-dev/presentation-shell-gotchas.md) — stale bus snapshots, wire lifecycle, authority split, scene shell vs catalog prefab, projector tests.

**Distinct from:** [centralized-ui-services.mdc](centralized-ui-services.mdc) — modal `ICentralizedUiSurface` services (`ItemListInventory`, PopIn lifecycle). Bus shells carry **DTO snapshots**; many surfaces still co-own formation bind on the phase HUD.

## Before coding

1. Read **presentation-shell-gotchas** (symptom → cause → fix for #314-class bugs).
2. Confirm **surface delivery**: catalog prefab vs scene `I*Shell` on phase GO (bootstrap checklist).
3. Split **formation bind** (live `BattleState`) from **interactive chrome** (live controller when input-sensitive).

## Locked rules

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| Projector builds DTO from gameplay events | Adjudicate combat/hub rules in projector |
| Shell `Apply` / `PlayBeat` — display + BEM from DTO | `RequestTransition`, save writes, `CommandRail.SwapPanelContent` in shell |
| Wire projectors from `UiPresentationBridge` + **phase lifecycle** | `Unwire` global projector from phase HUD `OnDisable` |
| Phase HUD `RefreshRosters()` / live chrome when targeting matters | Gate formation bind on `UiPresentationBridge.Instance != null` |
| `RefreshRosterChrome` from **live** `CombatController` for targeting | `bridge.Current*` highlights on `OnTargetingChanged` (stale one frame) |
| Full `CombatRosterPresentationState.Clear()` on unwired publish | Partial DTO reset (slots cleared, flags linger) |
| Lazy-init in `Apply` if host publishes before `Awake` | Assume shell `OnEnable` before first bus snapshot |
| `Apply(bridge.Current*)` catch-up in shell `OnEnable` | Duplicate chrome refresh on HUD **and** shell without `IfNotOnBus` guard |

## Review checklist

Reject shell/bus PRs that still have:

| Smell | Example |
|-------|---------|
| Stale DTO targeting | `ApplyHighlightsAndStats(bridge.CurrentCombatRoster)` on `OnTargetingChanged` |
| `UsesBus` kills direct refresh | `if (bridge != null) return` around `RefreshRosters()` |
| HUD owns projector wire | `CombatHudView.OnDisable` → `CombatRosterProjector.Unwire()` |
| Missing scene shell | `CombatRoster` catalog `shellPrefab: null` but no `CombatRosterScreenShell` on CombatHud |
| Gameplay in shell | `Apply` calls `CombatController.SelectTarget` |
| Projector test without phase | `Wire(combat, gameState: null)` when builder gates on `GamePhase.Combat` |

## Agent workflow

- **Shell / projector / bridge wiring PR:** read [presentation-shell-gotchas](../docs/04-dev/presentation-shell-gotchas.md) end-to-end before diff review.
- **Touches centralized modal + bus:** also run skill **`audit-centralized-ui-services`** (game repo) — PopIn traps stay in [centralized-ui-gotchas](centralized-ui-gotchas.md).

